 strong to get that value. They called 600 last time. Betting 1200 seems like a solid, balanced bet to get paid and maximize my win. I bet 1200.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: I possess a Queen-high Flush (Ah, Qh, 7h, 6h, 5h), which is the second-best possible hand configuration, losing only to a player holding the King of Hearts (who would have an Ace-King high flush). A Straight Flush is impossible for the opponent because I hold the 5h, which would be required for any straight flush combination on this board (3h, 4d, 6h, 7h, Ah - specifically the gap between 3, 6, 7). The opponent showed aggression on the flop but slowed down (check-called) on the turn and checked the river. This line is consistent with a lower flush or a made hand that is now scared of the 4-flush board. There are significantly more lower hearts (J, T, 9, 8, 4, 2) in the deck than the single King of Hearts that beats me. Therefore, betting for value is the correct play to extract chips from these inferior hands.\n\nReason: With the second nuts and a high probability that the opponent holds a worse hand (possibly a lower flush) rather than the absolute nuts, checking back would miss value. A bet of 1200 (approx. half pot) is sized to be called by worse flushes while controlling risk.\n\nAnswer: 1200'}
